 "about": "Real job and contract items per trade (PROJ and job-contract model). `rel` = reference price in a common currency (normalised on install so share x rel adds up to the trade's going ticket and the books never move), `share` = relative customers, `h` = person-hours of labour in the job, `crew` = people on it (roles of tables.json ROLES), `mat` and `sub` = materials and subcontractors as shares of the price before calibration (calibrated so the whole menu weighs the books' mat+sub traits, or cogs for handy and security), `mk` = markup the quote puts on materials, `lead` = days until the crew can start, `co` = call-out (arrives within a day), `wr` = share of jobs that need a warranty callback, `wm` = warranty months, `ph` = phases [name, share of price, share of that phase that is subcontracted], `visits`/`period`/`churn` = recurring plan or contract (hours per period for the guard contract), `buy` = stocked item bought at that share of its price. `extra` = add-item catalogue. `fteHours` = hours a full-time person works a week. `callbackHours` = share of a job's hours a callback takes. `onCost` = employer cost on top of pay.",
